      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CADUCEUS (2) sets the standard after winning his only race start at Balaklava, scoring in CL1 company over this trip on soft ground despite starting at generous odds. The six-month break is offset by two trial wins since, including one at Oakbank two weeks ago, and he has already beaten BLANDFORD BARON. BLANDFORD BARON (1) is the main danger if the freshen-up has him back on song; his two runs before the break were mixed, but a comfortable Balaklava trial and proven 1000m record keep him in the race. ONLY ONE RULER (3) has been safely held in BM60 and BM64 grade at this track, yet the drop into this CL1 gives him a better platform and the leading track jockey-trainer combination adds weight to his claims. ZEN REBEL (4) rounds out the small field.",
